      "memo_md": "# Decision memo: why did the on-time rate drop? (run zetaris-example-002)\nTop cause: **carrier_sla_breach** in carrier=CarrierB, region=North (estimated share of the excess late shipments vs the baseline rate: 104%; above 100% means other segments improved).\n\n- Question: Did the Home week South promotion cause the drop in on-time delivery between 2026-10-01 and 2026-10-14 compared with 2026-09-15 to 2026-09-30?\n- Baseline 2026-09-15..2026-09-30 vs period 2026-10-01..2026-10-14\n- Resolution: resolved\n- Data: SYNTHETIC labelled dataset (generated by scripts/make_data.py; planted causes)\n- Backends: data=zetaris-jdbc [on_time_rate], meterless=meterless-bridge (vendored engines via node), model provider=nightshift\n\n## Summary (model-written, numbers re-found by the traceability check)\nCarrierB's on-time rate in the North region collapsed from 93.0% in the baseline window (2026-09-15 to 2026-09-30) to 44.2% in the period window (2026-10-01 to 2026-10-14). A promotional hypothesis (PROMO-HOME-SOUTH) for the home category in the South region was investigated and refuted; its dates overlapped but it accounted for only 49 shipments with 3 late deliveries and a negative share of excess late. The model verdict confirms the promotion did not drive the North region carrier breach.\n\n## Findings (each passed the traceability check: cited rows and numbers re-found in the data; not independently verified as true)\n- On-time rate for carrier=CarrierB, region=North was 44.2% in the period window (2026-10-01..2026-10-14). Rows: S000977, S000979, S001028, S001040, S001068\n- On-time rate for carrier=CarrierB, region=North was 93.0% in the baseline window (2026-09-15..2026-09-30). Rows: S000014, S000021, S000024, S000032, S000045\n\n## Discarded alternatives\n- Promotion PROMO-HOME-SOUTH: dates overlap the period, but its shipments account for 0% of the excess late shipments (3 of 49). Refuted.\n\n## Confidence: 100/100\n- Formula: round(100*(0.45*C + 0.35*A + 0.20*(1-R))); C=1.0, A=1.0, R=0.0; caps: none\n\n## Recommended actions\n- Review the SLA performance of CarrierB in North and consider rerouting.\n\n## Limitations\n- Synthetic data. Model calls: 23 ok, 0 fell back to deterministic rules.\n- Evidence graph: meterless-hmem (vendored reference, via bridge); Markovian status: completed.\n\n## Run report (tokens, cost, latency)\n- Provider: nightshift (wall clock and latencies: report JSON)\n- Model calls: 23 ok, 0 fell back; tokens 21120 (prompt 19985, completion 1135)\n- Cost: metered by Meterless/Nightshift (not visible to this app)\n- S1 filter: 941 projected vs 245 sent (696 avoided, whitespace tokens (approx.))\n- planner / nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b: 1 ok, 0 failed, 382+27 tok\n- retriever / nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b: 9 ok, 0 failed, 10404+727 tok\n- s1_filter / nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b: 6 ok, 0 failed, 4538+172 tok\n- evidence_evaluator / nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b: 5 ok, 0 failed, 3341+45 tok\n- cause_analyst / nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b: 1 ok, 0 failed, 505+13 tok\n- writer / nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b: 1 ok, 0 failed, 815+151 tok\n"
